  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Atomics has $436M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. General Atomics won 115 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $3.8M, and obligations are up 9.1% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $384M to General Atomics in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy is the second-largest buyer, obligating $47M, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $5.1M. Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing is the largest NAICS market for General Atomics, with $376M in obligations. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the next largest market, with $47M. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing and Ship Building and Repairing are smaller current markets, with $5.2M and $5.1M respectively. Historical obligations show year-by-year activity: FY21 $261M, FY22 $229M, FY23 $456M, FY24 $240M, and FY25 $400M.",
    "sections": [
